            <ArticleTitle>[A boy with abdominal pain, fever and liver abcesses].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A7231</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 18-year-old male with right lower abdominal pain and elevated infection parameters is diagnosed with an abdominal abscess, multiple liver abscesses and a thrombus in his portal vein. This combination of findings leads to the diagnosis 'foie appendiculaire', a complicated form of appendicitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
